{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md'","aggregated_output":"# Source-grounded consensus investigation\n\nCandidate records a sourced question, protections and unknowns. Obligation states an applicable responsibility; Check supplies a test, schedule or model; Evidence records attributed observations. Source explanation and bounded negative results are useful outcomes; an obligation is not confirmation.\n\nUse the authoritative activity_roles in research.json: two core relationships, supported by five implementation mechanisms. A question may concern either core relationship. Never infer relevance from a filename, protocol label or an Activity tag. Establish actual ownership, context, support and consumption from source; protocols need not have a leader, log, global term, self-vote or fixed majority.\n\nFirst build a sourced overall explanation of both core lines and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Trace a representative operation from entry through actual owners, support production, identity and eligibility, aggregation and decision conditions to recording, propagation, application or public completion. Trace how this implementation acquires, changes and loses its context or authority, including how old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions survive, exit or are reconfirmed. Follow real callees, producers and consumers in both directions; compare important reject, stale, retry and asynchronous paths. General CFT knowledge supplies questions, not attributed requirements or invented target behavior, including when protocol=none.\n\nRead the membership, history, recovery or completion mechanisms needed to explain these paths now; deeper backend variants can remain open. A Behavior describes an actual owner, trigger, guards, effects and alternatives. A Fact states the weakest assertion the implementation establishes for an identified object and context. Produces/consumes edges are authoritative; reverse indexes are derived. Save partial maps and early anomalies as sourced Surfaces without claiming readiness for focused investigation. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: an unread failure variant may be a detail; unexplained decision formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks the initial backbone. Mark unavailable source or permission boundaries explicitly. Usable is a sourced judgment, not proof or a demand to read every file. Keep the overview about mechanisms and important connections; local details belong in Behavior/Fact/Surface. Execution progress belongs to CheckRun and its current assessment, not overview unknowns.\n\nOnly a user-configured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary before this overall explanation. activity_focus alone does not waive either initial core line. Otherwise use next_objective in research.json: recover the missing backbone, then choose a local discriminator. A usable overview and the first Candidate may be submitted together. Local exploration requires neither a fabricated Fact nor an obligation.\n\nSelect one principal Fact lifecycle and a concrete A1/A2 relationship. question.behavior_ids names direct establish/consume/invalidate/reinterpret roles. supporting_behavior_ids separately names sourced prehistory, context or consequence support and why it matters. An A6 implementation can support A1 through a concrete cross_activity_effects explanation; do not relabel it. Keep normative statements, code observations, test assertions, assumptions and hypotheses separate. Source identity does not prove meaning.\n\nUse existing question, Behavior owner/context and Harness legality to identify the selected entry, serialization owner, storage/application/network duties and the observation that means completion. Shared internals do not imply identical API permissions; neither high nor low level is inherently preferable. If a needed permission belongs to another entry, compare explaining the correspondence, using that entry directly, and cheap exploration before fixing a heavy check. Choose the path that answers the limiting premise with obtainable evidence.\n\nSeparate requirement, producer, prefix, legal same-execution history and observed endpoint gaps. Calls do not establish callee effects; independent executions do not form one history. Explain whether protections run, are finitely delayed or omitted with sourced noninterference reasoning. A constructed prefix may be justified by actual producers without starting at process birth; direct assignment of critical state remains conditional. Actively investigate the tractable gap that most changes the current judgment.\n\nShared Behavior/Fact relationships and parent links do not propagate conclusions. Ground obligations in applicable expectations, not code differences. Express relations over objects and contexts; concrete identities and timings belong to Check, while applicability-defining modes, counts and faults belong to Claim/Scope. A small test does not weaken the requirement; abstraction does not prove global safety. Source explanation needs no fabricated execution, and a local violation need not prove its suspected cause or wider consequence.\n\nKeep the Candidate and Unit for unchanged requirements and scope. First fix the execution error while preserving observation names, identities, predicates and legality; a small helper bug does not require an encoding refactor or a preliminary review of the failed version. Fixed harness changes still need a new artifact, execution and current correspondence review. Answer existing issues explicitly. Driver premise changes use sourced repair_issue_ids; observation/oracle changes use encoding revision; applicability/meaning changes use F2 and dependency expansion uses F3. Wider consequences may form independent questions.\n\nAt explanation, bounded completion, confirmation, pause or repair completion, save the new sourced answer and next discriminator in feedback. A source protection may settle a suspicion without a test; execute when actual production, scheduling or completion can change the judgment. Add stable producer/consumer relationships to AuditSpec before later questions depend on them; keep input-specific observations in execution/feedback. Reuse adequate maps and update core_overview only for important connections. Independent additions preserve old results; actual counterevidence challenges its specific interpretation. Read earlier handoffs through their locators; remaining is historical. Update current semantic unknowns through question_updates; CheckRun owns execution progress.\n\nUse Codex search, editing and permitted feedback within the snapshot/draft boundary. Choose direct experiments or optional models for the actual discriminator. Prefer finishing a concrete accepted check; justify a useful switch with pause/feedback. Near the deadline submit small complete sourced feedback for new knowledge; no extra closing report is needed to repeat saved results. The controller reports natural expiry from retained state. Never manufacture closure with an incomplete review.\n\nEvidence of one complete violation and completion of all required scenarios are different quantifiers. Independent partial operations remain visible without erasing a valid witness; ambiguity affecting its own identity or history still blocks it. A passing process, model holds, provisional review, absent issues or locally checked Unit is not overall correctness. Stop honestly within authorization [REDACTED] budgets; the controller records pending work even if the last explanation is incomplete.\n\nConsensus safety has priority, with liveness under explicit environment/fault/scheduling or deadline assumptions. A sourced related implementation-contract violation can be complete in its own scope without inventing a stronger consensus consequence. General code issues stay secondary. Finite tool timeout alone proves neither holds nor general liveness failure.\n\nAfter each local disposition use the overview and relationship navigation to choose a useful next step: a remaining premise, another actual consumer/context of the same Fact, or an independent sourced discriminator. This is not a required three-item form or subsystem rotation. Local obstacles do not block every relationship; mapped does not mean settled. Record the chosen unknown, protection and expected information gain in existing trigger_rationale/feedback, without another selection product. Reading, explanation, exploration, repair, review or knowledge retention can be worthwhile without promising a complete new finding. Reuse valid maps and checks; new work within authorization [REDACTED] no further user instruction.\n\npending_work is selected execution/review debt; frontier.comparison_refs is the minimum stop accounting, not a candidate whitelist or coverage proof. Unreferenced behaviors and historical handoffs are navigation, not mandatory tasks. Settled automatic pauses need no reopening; genuine unresolved premises remain. A reasoned early stop may leave unknowns and budget when the best known steps cannot yield useful retained information within current boundaries. The Agent judges value; structure checks references and explicit consistency, not the truth of actionable=false. Preserve independent results, permission limits and fresh-run isolation; runtime interruption facts belong to the controller.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\nfor id,file,a,b,kind in [('entry','rawnode.go',31,180,'code_observation'),('ready-contract','node.go',50,178,'interface_statement'),('reply-queue','raft.go',512,599,'code_observation'),('reset-append','raft.go',778,846,'code_observation'),('roles','raft.go',891,971,'code_observation'),('term-filter','raft.go',1085,1175,'code_observation'),('ready-release','rawnode.go',176,199,'code_observation'),('storage-envelope','rawnode.go',202,281,'code_observation'),('apply-accept','rawnode.go',390,450,'code_observation'),('advance','rawnode.go',477,494,'code_observation')]:\n sources.append(dict(id=id,file=file,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=kind))\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain initial source-grounded entry, persistence and term-transition observations while the required two-core backbone remains incomplete.',sources=sources,feedback=dict(ref_ids=[x['id'] for x in sources],understanding='updated',answered='Interface expectations: Node.Propose explicitly permits proposals to be lost and assigns retries to the caller; Ready assigns persistence-before-send duties and distinguishes synchronous Advance from asynchronous storage responses. Code observations: RawNode is thread-unsafe, Propose dispatches MsgProp, and network Step rejects unexpected local messages and unknown peer responses. raft.appendEntry assigns the current term and successive indexes, appends locally, and sends a self-directed MsgAppResp through send. send queues append and vote responses in msgsAfterAppend, including rejected responses. Synchronous Ready exposes remote responses under its storage contract, while acceptReady records self responses for Advance; asynchronous Ready builds a LocalAppendThread envelope carrying dependent responses. This is a storage handoff, not independent proof of durability. reset clears votes, remote replication progress and readOnly tracking; becomeCandidate increments term and self-votes; becomeLeader resets same-term tracking and appends an empty entry. Step handles higher terms with explicit pre-vote and lease exceptions. Its lower-term MsgStorageAppendResp branch does not stabilize entries but still dispatches snapshot completion to appliedSnap. newStorageAppendRespMsg attaches current raft term in addition to entry index/term; newStorageApplyRespMsg deliberately has term zero. Inference: old entry-write completion and committed application completion have distinct validity contexts, so a common stale-response predicate would be unjustified. These observations do not establish quorum formation, durable recovery, or consensus correctness.',remaining=['Core gap: follow proposal forwarding and leader guards through follower append production, reply consumption, tracker quorum aggregation and raftLog commit guards.', 'Core gap: trace campaign/vote eligibility, quorum loss and transfer, configuration activation and joint quorum consumers.', 'Core gap: follow committed entries, snapshots, storage reconstruction and old pending read handling through actual callees before declaring core_overview usable.'],rationale='Next recover the proposal-to-commit and election-to-authority paths, then connect membership and recovery. Existing reply queuing and term filtering are concrete protections to preserve; tracing their consumers will distinguish eligibility from mere notification without selecting a premature Candidate.'))\nwith open('submission.json','w') as f: json.dump(s,f,indent=2)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
